<Base title="Privacy and supported data" description="Privacy boundary and limits for the local JSONL tool and the unhosted Astro starter." section="Privacy">
 <section class="copy-page"><span class="eyebrow">DATA / PRIVACY</span><h1>Local processing by design.</h1><p>The bundled JSONL tool reads selected files through browser File APIs and processes them in a same-origin Web Worker. It does not send your JSONL records to an application backend. No external advertising, analytics or third-party script is embedded in the example.</p><h2>File retention</h2><p>Files stay in browser memory for the active session; transformed output is a Blob URL that is revoked when input or options change, the workspace is reset, or the page is left. The downloaded file is retained by your browser and operating system according to your own settings.</p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>This source-only starter is not publicly deployed, does not offer accounts, synchronization, backups or persistent cloud storage, and cannot make claims about a hosting provider's network logs until that provider is selected. Any future deployment must update this notice for actual server logs, analytics, cookies, support contacts and local legal requirements.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>Do not upload sensitive production data to unknown hosted copies. JSONL values are inserted into preview text nodes, not HTML. You should still review normalized output and test for downstream consumer behavior.</p></section>
</Base>
